# field_bridge: Chrome extension + local WebSocket bridge to read and edit an authorized field.

# --- structure
The program "field_bridge" contains the process "bridge", the process "cmd", the service worker "background", the content script "content", the page script "main-world" and the window "popup".
The process "bridge" runs in the execution context "python asyncio".
The process "cmd" runs in the execution context "python asyncio".
The service worker "background" runs in the execution context "service worker".
The content script "content" runs in the execution context "isolated world".
The page script "main-world" runs in the execution context "MAIN world".
The window "popup" runs in the execution context "extension popup".
The process "bridge" contains the map "pending", the set "watchers" and the counter "id_counter".
The process "cmd" contains the message "command".
The service worker "background" contains the timer "field-bridge-reconnect".
The content script "content" contains the text field "authorized field", the state machine "selection mode", the map "pending main-world" and the key-value store "chrome.storage.local".
The page script "main-world" contains the set "watching" and the function "getDiagnostics".

# --- channel and messages
The process "bridge" listens on the websocket endpoint "ws://127.0.0.1:8797".
The process "cmd" connects to the websocket endpoint "ws://127.0.0.1:8797".
The service worker "background" connects to the websocket endpoint "ws://127.0.0.1:8797".
The process "cmd" sends the message "command" to the process "bridge".
The process "bridge" forwards the message "command" to the service worker "background".
The service worker "background" sends the message "command" to the content script "content".
The content script "content" sends the event "field-bridge-request" to the page script "main-world" through the execution context "DOM window".
The page script "main-world" sends the event "field-bridge-response" to the content script "content" through the execution context "DOM window".
The page script "main-world" sends the event "field-bridge-change" to the content script "content" through the execution context "DOM window".
The content script "content" sends the message "change event" to the service worker "background".
The service worker "background" sends the message "change event" to the process "bridge".
The process "bridge" forwards the message "change event" to the set "watchers".
The window "popup" sends the message "start-select" to the content script "content".
The window "popup" injects the content script "content" and the page script "main-world" into the tab "active tab".
The service worker "background" injects the content script "content" and the page script "main-world" into the tab "each tab".

# --- state and keys
The map "pending" is keyed by the value "request id".
The map "pending main-world" is keyed by the value "request id".
The key-value store "chrome.storage.local" is keyed by the value "origin plus path".
The key-value store "chrome.storage.local" is persistent.
The timer "field-bridge-reconnect" repeats every "5 s".
The content script "content" is idempotent.
The page script "main-world" is idempotent.
The process "bridge" changes the map "pending".
The process "bridge" changes the set "watchers".

# --- selection state machine
The state machine "selection mode" has the states "idle" and "selecting".
The state machine "selection mode" starts in the state "idle".
The window "popup" moves the state machine "selection mode" from the state "idle" to the state "selecting".
The content script "content" moves the state machine "selection mode" from the state "selecting" to the state "idle".

# --- invariants
When the service worker "background" connects to the process "bridge", the process "bridge" replaces the connection "previous extension".
If the message "first message" times out, the process "bridge" closes the connection "client".
The message "first message" times out after "5 s".
The map "pending" times out after "10 s".
The map "pending main-world" times out after "8 s".
The service worker "background" picks the tab "first tab with authorized field".
The service worker "background" does not pick the tab "active tab".
The content script "content" never reads the value "window.ace".
The page script "main-world" reads the value "window.ace".
If the page script "main-world" changes the text field "authorized field", the page script "main-world" dispatches the event "input" and the event "change".
If the service worker "background" does not connect to the process "bridge", the process "bridge" sends the message "extension not connected" to the process "cmd".
If the timer "field-bridge-reconnect" times out, the service worker "background" connects to the process "bridge".
